text:
What is the output of the following code written in C?
void main()
{
printf("%d%d%d",62,062,0x62);
}

Consider the following segment of C++ code.
int j, n;
for(j=1;j<=n; )
j=j*2;
What is the number of comparisons made in the execution of the loop for any n > 0?

What is the output of the given java code?
byte x = 64, y;
y = (byte) (x << 4);
system.out.println(y);

What is the output of the code written in C?
void main()
{
printf("%d",7%-3);
printf("%d",-7%3);
}

Which statement in this code is unreachable switch(x)?
{
case 1:
a1=100;
case 2:
a2=1000;
a3=10;
break;
a4=10000;
}

What is the output of the code written in C?
void main()
{
int k, val=1;
k= ++val*++val;
printf("%d",k);
}

What is the output of the following java code?
int m = 1000;
int k = 3000;
while (+ + m < – – k);
System.out.println(m);

What is the output of the code written in C?
void main()
{
int k, v;
k=(v=20,v+2);
printf("%d",k);
}

What is the output of the following JAVA code?
String s = “exam:” + 9 + 9 + 9;
System.out.println(s);

What is the output of the code written in C?
void main()
{
int k=8, v=8,i;
i=k/++v;
printf("%d\n",i);
}

Consider the following C declaration. Assume that objects of data type short, float and long occupy 2 bytes, 4 bytes and 8 bytes respectively.
What is memory requirement for variable t?
struct {
short a[5];
union{
float v;
long z;}
u;
}t;

What is the output of the following ‘C’ language statements?
#include<stdio.h>
int main(){
int a=10,b=20,*p1=&a,*p2=&b;
printf("Before : **p1=%d **p2=%d",*p1,*p2);
*p1=*p1+*p2;
*p2=*p1-*p2;
*p1=*p1-*p2;
printf("\nAfter : **p1=%d **p2=%d",*p1,*p2);
return 0;
}

What is the expected output of the following Java code?
public class operators {
  public static void main(String[] args)
  {
    int a = 5;
    int b = 7;
    System.out.println("a&b = " + (a & b));
  }
}

